 "poem": "XIII. OMNES DE ILLUMINUS in\nThe World and the Soul to die, alas!\nThou hast ne'er been born a man of spirit;\nNot even thy golden age was happy.\nNot happy was the realm of our\nLonely night - and wilder fires were\nForlornly blazed, till one such flame afar\nShone burning on the sun's bright brow, our\nMorning star! - but no immortal flame\nHad anything like thee; yet our\nStars must burn for ever; and 'twere fatal,\nSome 'gainst some, that thine own image cannot",
